# Vercel production deploy

Production URL: https://hireflow-ai-hireflowgroup1.vercel.app

Vercel deploys from the **`main`** branch (GitHub → Vercel integration).

## After every push that should reach production

When the user asks to push, deploy, or ship to Vercel (or does not specify a branch-only push):

1. Push the feature branch to `origin`.
2. **Merge into `main`** (fast-forward or merge commit) and **`git push origin main`**.
3. Confirm Vercel build triggered (GitHub commit on `main` is sufficient when integration is connected).
4. Optionally verify key routes respond (e.g. `/outreach`, `/ai-recruiter` → expect auth redirect, not 404).

## Do not

- Force-push `main`
- Skip `main` merge when user wants changes on the Vercel link
- Commit `.github/workflows/` unless user has GitHub `workflow` OAuth scope

## Env vars on Vercel

After schema or env changes, remind user to update Vercel project env and run `supabase db push` for migrations.
